# Request for Software

## What

- A program to sync an RPi's system clock when a user SSHes into it

    - Automation is preferred but not required

    - Don't automate if automation would slow down scan speed


## When

- Must be finished before 2026-08-01



## How

- Should probably be written in Bash

- Must be CLI only (no graphical interface!)

- Must be executable (the tool you want is `chmod +x`)



## Compatibility

This must interface with:

- Humans (see "Interface", below)

- An automated startup script, cron job, .profile command, or similar

This code must run on:

- Ubuntu 24.04 Server

It would be nice if this code also ran on:

- Ubuntu 20 (whatever version the old RPis have got on them)



## Interface

Here is how this package will be used:

`cd *wherever*`

`./sync-clock.sh`



 ## Detailed Specification

The program must run on an RPi

 When run, the program must check if an external computer is connected to it by SSH

    If it is not, the program should wait until the external computer is connected, using as little compute power as possible

    If it is...

When the RPi is connected, via SSH, to a computer or Android mobile phone (specs available upon request), the script must update the RPi's system clock to match the system clock of the other computer

    Ideally, the other computer should not need to have any script running on it to make this work

    If another script proves necessary, it must be able to run on Ubuntu 20, Ubuntu 24, and Termux on Android 13, 
    and separate interfaces must be developed, documented, and maintained for each

This program must be documented, both in comments and in the Summer Project Log, and, if applicable, in the textbook, in such detail that a newcomer with only minimal 
system knowledge would be able to understand your code and write an extension to it adding some undefined additional functionality.

After all functionality has been achieved, the relevant installer scripts must be updated to install this package, and these changes must be documented also.

